{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.plancherel_W_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.plancherel_W_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingWeightMarkovPinning.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**Capstone — `W_λ` is excluded, so the binding weight is `y_λ`.** Instantiate\n`asymmetric_weight_ne_symmetric` on the `(3)`/`(1,1,1)` pair with the Plancherel weight symmetric there\n(`Wq` equal, since the hook products are equal — `Wq_symmetric_of_prod_eq`) and the Markov weight\nasymmetric (`markov_y_asymmetric_n3`): no weight system equal to the symmetric `W_λ` can match the\nasymmetric Markov weights. scope-(b) structural exclusion; the weight is pinned to `y_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.markov_y_asymmetric_n3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.markov_y_asymmetric_n3","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingWeightMarkovPinning.lean#L55-L57","doc":"**The Markov weight is asymmetric on the `(3)`/`(1,1,1)` conjugate pair** (`y_(3) ≠ y_(1,1,1)`):\n`0.41539579 ≠ 0.022744946`. This is the chirality the Plancherel `W_λ` (symmetric) cannot supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.asymmetric_weight_ne_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.asymmetric_weight_ne_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingWeightMarkovPinning.lean#L46-L53","doc":"**A conjugation-symmetric weight cannot be the (asymmetric) Markov weight.** If a candidate weight\n`W` is symmetric on a conjugate pair (`W a = W b`) while the Markov weight `y` is asymmetric there\n(`y a ≠ y b`), then `y ≠ W` as weight systems (`¬ ∀ i, y i = W i`) — so `W` is not the Markov weight.\nThis is the structural exclusion of `W_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.Wq_symmetric_of_prod_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.Wq_symmetric_of_prod_eq","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingWeightMarkovPinning.lean#L39-L43","doc":"**`W_λ` is conjugation-symmetric.** The hook-length multiset is transpose-invariant\n(`hooks(λ) = hooks(λ')`, verified ≤ n=7), so the hook products agree (`P₁ = P₂`); hence\n`W_λ = W_{λ'}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.Wq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingWeightMarkovPinning.Wq","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingWeightMarkovPinning.lean#L34-L36","doc":"The q-Plancherel / Schur-Weyl weight as a function of the hook product `P = ∏[h_x]` and\n`F = [n]_q!`: `W_λ = d_q(λ)²/[n]! = [n]!/(∏[h])²`. It depends on `λ` ONLY through the hook product. ","signatureChunk":0}]}